# 1. Alert Sorting — Corrected and Optimized Pseudocode

## A. Corrected Algorithm: Insertion Sort

**Input:** List of alerts containing alert ID and severity.

**Output:** Alerts sorted by descending severity.

```text
ALGORITHM CORRECTED_SORT_ALERTS(alerts)

    FOR i ← 1 TO LENGTH(alerts) - 1
        current ← alerts[i]
        j ← i - 1

        WHILE j >= 0 AND alerts[j].severity < current.severity
            alerts[j + 1] ← alerts[j]
            j ← j - 1
        END WHILE

        alerts[j + 1] ← current
    END FOR

    RETURN alerts

END ALGORITHM
```

## B. Optimized Algorithm: Built-in Sorting

```text
ALGORITHM OPTIMIZED_SORT_ALERTS(alerts)

    SORT alerts by severity in descending order
    RETURN sorted alerts

END ALGORITHM
```

**Time Complexity:**
- Corrected insertion sort: Best case O(n), worst case O(n²).
- Optimized built-in sorting: Typically O(n log n).

**Purpose:** Correctly arrange security alerts from highest severity to lowest severity without losing or duplicating alert records.
